      "description": "As a registered Shopper, I want to add a new delivery address from within checkout, so that I can ship to a location not already saved in my account.\nThis component represents the add new address state of the delivery address section for logged-in users (Image 6). It is reached by selecting \"Add New\" from the collapsed dropdown (SFCC-334) or \"Add New Address\" from the expanded list (SFCC-335). At the top of this state a dropdown field labelled \"New address\" is shown — this allows the customer to navigate back to their saved addresses without leaving checkout. Below it the full address form is rendered with pre-filled first and last name (from account), Country dropdown, address autocomplete field, PO Box / Parcel Locker warning text, phone country prefix dropdown (see SFCC-339), and mobile field. Address autocomplete is powered by Google Places API (see SFCC-337, SFCC-64). Manual address entry fallback is a separate component (see SFCC-338). Upon order completion the new address is saved to the customer's address book. Surface: PWA Kit / SFCC checkout page. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit. Depends on CFD-025, CFD-027, CFD-028, CFD-029, CFD-031. Cross-epic dependency: SFCC-64 (Google Address Autocomplete), My Account address book epic.",
