      "id": "18750",
      "key": "SFCC-404",
      "summary": "Cart – Page-Level Error Banner Component",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see a clear page-level error message when an action in my cart cannot be completed, so that I understand what has gone wrong and can take the appropriate action to resolve it.\\n\\nThis component is a reusable page-level error banner that appears at the top of the cart page when a cart action fails or a rule is violated. Known triggers include: attempting to move an item to the wishlist that already exists in the wishlist (SFCC-272); exceeding the maximum quantity of 3 units per SKU (SFCC-250); an item becoming out of stock in the cart (SFCC-282); checkout CTA disabled due to an OOS item (CAI-035). The banner renders with a red X icon and error message text. Dismissal behaviour: the banner must support both manual dismiss (customer clicks X to close) and auto-dismiss on resolution (e.g. max quantity error clears automatically when the customer adjusts quantity to within the allowed limit). Error message copy is configurable. Designs not yet available - Figma is leading.\nPROD Screenshot",
