    {
      "id": "19055",
      "key": "SFCC-650",
      "summary": "pdp/add-to-bag",
      "description": "As a Developer, I want a reusable \npdp/add-to-bag\n React component built for the Zimmermann PWA Kit, so that it can be consumed by the PDP and any other page-level stories that require add-to-bag functionality.\nThe component renders using the base Button component (Primary, Large) from the Zimmermann design system. It wraps it with add-to-bag-specific interaction logic: size selection validation, stock state awareness, loading state during cart API call, and inline error messaging. Cart API integration is in scope for this story. Maximum purchase quantity enforcement is handled separately in SFCC-196.",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a shopper lands on a PDP and no size has been selected, when the page loads, then the Add to Bag CTA is displayed but disabled."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a shopper attempts to click Add to Bag without selecting a size, when the click is registered, then the button remains inactive and a \"Size required\" inline message is displayed."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a shopper selects an in-stock size, when the selection is registered, then the Add to Bag CTA becomes active and enabled."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given a shopper clicks Add to Bag with a valid size selected, when the action is triggered, then the cart API call is made and the button displays a loading state while the call is in flight."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given the cart API call completes successfully, when the response is received, then the item is confirmed as added to bag and the appropriate success state is shown."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given the cart API call fails, when the error response is received, then an inline error message is displayed and the CTA returns to its enabled state so the shopper can retry."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a product is a one-size item, when the component is rendered, then the size is treated as pre-selected and the Add to Bag CTA is active on page load."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. The component accepts size selection state and stock status as props — it does not manage size selection itself; that is owned by pdp/size-selector ("
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-648#icft=SFCC-648"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ")."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given a keyboard user tabs to the Add to Bag CTA, when the component receives focus, then a visible focus ring is displayed per the design system spec."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "10. Given the CTA is in a disabled state, when a screen reader user reaches it, then it is announced as unavailable so the user understands action is required before proceeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "11. Given an inline error or success message is displayed, when it is triggered, then the message is announced via an ARIA live region without requiring the user to navigate to it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "12. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA as the minimum accessibility standard."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "19053",
      "key": "SFCC-649",
      "summary": "Cart – Guest to Authenticated Basket Merge on Sign-In",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want my guest cart to merge with my account basket when I sign in, so that I do not lose any items I added before authenticating.\nWhen a guest Shopper signs in during or before checkout, their guest basket is merged with their authenticated account basket. This story covers the merge logic and the resulting cart state. Maximum quantity rules apply post-merge (3 units per SKU). Depends on SFCC-279 for basket persistence configuration.",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "AC1. Guest Items Only — Transfer to Authenticated Basket",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "strong"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "062ecd2a22c6"
              }
