      "description": "As a guest Shopper, I want to enter my delivery address in a form, so that my order can be shipped to my chosen location.\nThis component appears on the checkout delivery step for unauthenticated (guest) users (Images 1 and 9). It is the guest-only state of the delivery address form — no saved address dropdown is shown. Fields rendered: First name, Last name, Country dropdown (pre-populated from storefront locale, editable), address autocomplete text field (\"Start typing your address*\"), PO Box / Parcel Locker warning text, phone country prefix dropdown (AU +61 default, see SFCC-339), mobile number text input, and a \"For delivery purposes only\" checkbox. The country dropdown includes a \"Country not found? CLICK HERE\" fallback link. Address autocomplete is powered by Google Places API (see SFCC-337, SFCC-64). Manual address entry fallback is a separate component (see SFCC-338). Surface: PWA Kit / SFCC checkout page. Owned by: SFCC/PWA Kit. Depends on CFD-022, CFD-024, CFD-025, CFD-027, CFD-031. Cross-epic dependency: SFCC-64 (Google Address Autocomplete).",
