    {
      "id": "18581",
      "key": "SFCC-297",
      "summary": "PDP UI — Find in Boutique Button and Slide-In Panel",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper,\nI want \nto find which boutiques have my size in stock directly from the PDP,\nso that\n I can visit a store to try or purchase the item if I prefer not to order online.\nPicture for reference (Figma leading): \nThis story covers the PWA Kit frontend component for Find in Boutique on the PDP. It includes the Find in Boutique button display on eligible products, the modal/flyout UI showing per-boutique stock availability for the selected size, and all boutique availability states. The real-time OMS call to NewStore via MuleSoft and response caching logic are out of scope — covered in \nhttps://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-308\n . ",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a product is eligible for Find in Boutique, when the shopper lands on the PDP, then a Find in Boutique button/CTA is displayed."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given the shopper clicks Find in Boutique, when the modal opens, then it displays the product image, name, colour and price at the top."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given the modal is open, when no size has been selected, then a size selector dropdown is shown with a prompt to select a size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given the shopper selects a size in the modal, when boutique results are returned, then each boutique is listed with its name, address, open/closed status, distance, and one of three availability states: Available / Low Stock / Out of Stock."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given a boutique row is collapsed, when the shopper clicks Explore Boutique, then it expands to show opening hours, phone number, email, Google Maps embed, and a Get Directions link."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given a boutique row is expanded, when the shopper clicks to collapse it, then the boutique details are hidden."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given the shopper clicks Get Directions for a boutique, when clicked, then Google Maps opens in a new tab with the route pre-populated to that boutique's address."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. Given the shopper clicks Use Location, when geolocation permission is granted, then the store locator field is populated with their current location and results are sorted by proximity."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given the shopper types a country, city, state or street into the location search field, when they submit, then boutique results are filtered and sorted by proximity to that location."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "10. Given no boutiques have the selected size in stock, when results are displayed, then a clear empty state message is shown."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "11. Given the modal is open on mobile, when rendered, then the modal displays in a full-width slide-up panel consistent with Zimmermann mobile design patterns."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "12. Given the shopper clicks the close (X) icon, when clicked, then the modal closes and the shopper is returned to the PDP."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "18567",
      "key": "SFCC-290",
      "summary": "Product Attributes – SFCC Full Attribute Set Definition & Configuration",
