    {
      "id": "18549",
      "key": "SFCC-272",
      "summary": "Cart Page – Cart Item - Remove Item and Move to Wishlist Line Item Actions",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to remove an item from my cart or move it to my wishlist directly from the cart page, so that I can manage my bag without losing products I may want to purchase later.\nBoth \"Remove\" and \"Wishlist\" actions appear as underlined links beneath each line item, consistent with Figma designs for desktop and mobile. All cart and wishlist state is managed by SFCC.\nImage for reference (figma leading):",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart, when they click Remove, then the item is immediately removed from the cart and the order summary updates accordingly."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given the cart had only one item and the Shopper removes it, when the removal completes, then the empty cart state is displayed as per "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-277#icft=SFCC-277",
                    "localId": "d7656ca5032c"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a Shopper has a line item in the cart with a quantity greater than 1, when they click Remove, then all units of that line item are removed from the cart in a single action."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given an Authenticated Shopper clicks Move to Wishlist on a line item with a quantity of 1, when the action completes, then the item is moved to their wishlist, removed from the cart, and a page-level success banner is displayed reading [Product Name] has been moved to your wishlist (see "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-405#icft=SFCC-405",
                    "localId": "d7ff385978cb"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " for banner component behaviour)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given an Authenticated Shopper has a quantity greater than 1 of a line item in their cart and clicks Move to Wishlist, when the action completes, then all units are removed from the cart, a single SKU is saved to the wishlist, and the page-level success banner displays [Product Name] has been moved to your wishlist (see "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-405#icft=SFCC-405",
                    "localId": "ef2815bd83c9"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " for banner component behaviour)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given an Authenticated Shopper clicks Move to Wishlist on a line item that already exists in their wishlist, when the action is attempted, then a page-level error banner is displayed reading “Selected product already exists in wishlist and the item remains in the cart” (see "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404#icft=SFCC-404",
                    "localId": "969f845b0e81"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " for banner component behaviour)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a Guest Shopper clicks Move to Wishlist on a line item, when the action is taken, then they are redirected to the login/registration page and the item remains in the cart until they authenticate."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. Given a Guest Shopper authenticates after being redirected, when they return to the cart, then the item is moved to their wishlist, removed from the cart, and a page-level success banner is displayed (see "
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-405#icft=SFCC-405",
                    "localId": "48165f0258d5"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " for banner component behaviour)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given a Shopper is on any device, when they interact with the Remove or Move to Wishlist actions, then both actions render and function correctly across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications."
                }
              ],
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "019a15db242e"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "18547",
      "key": "SFCC-270",
      "summary": "Cart Page – Cart Item - Product Information Display (Product Image, Name, Price, Colour, Size, Quantity)",
      "description": "As a Shopper, I want to see full product details for each item in my cart, so that I can review what I am purchasing before proceeding to checkout.\nEach line item on the cart page displays the product image, name, price, colour, size, and quantity. This applies across all storefronts on both desktop and mobile. All line item data is served from SFCC via the PWA Kit.\nNote: Gift Card Products will be covered in Gift Cards Epic. Non-Returnable/Refundable messaging will be covered in Returns/Refunds Epic.\nImage for reference (figma leading):",
      "status": {
        "name": "Ready For Review",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a Shopper has items in their cart, when they open the cart page, then each line item displays the product image."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a line item is rendered, when the page loads, then the product name is displayed adjacent to the image."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a line item is rendered, when the page loads, then the product price is displayed for that item."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given a line item is rendered, when the page loads, then the selected colour is displayed for that item."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given a line item is rendered, when the page loads, then the selected size is displayed for that item."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given a line item is rendered, when the page loads, then the current quantity is displayed with increment "
                },
                {
                  "type": "emoji",
                  "attrs": {
                    "shortName": ":plus:",
                    "id": "atlassian-plus",
                    "text": ":plus:",
                    "localId": "40e7e15985cc"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and decrement (–) controls either side."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a Shopper has multiple items in their cart, when the page loads, then all items are listed and each is individually identifiable."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. Given a Shopper views the cart on mobile, when the page renders, then all line item details (image, name, price, colour, size, quantity) are visible and no detail is truncated or hidden."
                }
              ],
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "76f5abf66720"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "18543",
      "key": "SFCC-269",
      "summary": "PLP Inline Grid Insert – Editorial Image",
      "description": "As a\n Shopper, \nI want\n to see a large-format editorial image with supporting text and a CTA inserted within the product grid as I browse, \nso that\n I can discover campaign stories and navigate to related editorial content alongside products.\nReference Image (Figma is leading):\nThis story covers the PWA build of the editorial image variant of the inline grid insert component. The insert occupies a single large-format slot within the product grid on category pages, spanning 2 product rows in height. The adjacent column displays an editorial title, body copy, and an optional CTA link in its upper portion, with regular product tiles below. Multiple inserts on the same page alternate between left and right positioning.\nThe component can be built with mock/hardcoded content at this stage — Contentful integration is covered in SFCC-204.\nThis story is one of three covering the inline grid insert variants.",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a category has been configured with an editorial image inline grid insert, when a shopper browses the product grid, then the insert renders at the configured position within the grid."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given the insert is positioned on the left, when the grid renders, then the large-format editorial image occupies the leftmost column spanning 2 product rows, with the editorial text block in the upper portion of the adjacent column and product tiles below it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given the insert is positioned on the right, when the grid renders, then the large-format editorial image occupies the rightmost column spanning 2 product rows, with the editorial text block in the upper portion of the adjacent column and product tiles below it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given the insert renders, when a shopper views it, then an editorial title and body copy are displayed in the upper portion of the adjacent column as per Figma."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given a CTA has been configured, when a shopper clicks it, then they are navigated to the linked destination (mock URL at this stage)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given no CTA has been configured, when a shopper views the insert, then no CTA is rendered and the layout remains intact."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a category has multiple inline grid inserts, when the grid renders, then inserts alternate between left and right positioning down the page."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. Given the insert is rendered on mobile, when the page loads, then the large-format editorial image renders full width with the editorial text block and product tiles continuing below it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given no editorial image inline grid insert has been configured for a category, when a shopper browses the product grid, then the full grid renders without interruption."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
